// Information on each "mode" in PGO.
// A mode in PGO derives from GCC modes.
// pgo_mode_e is also intended to contain information regarding where in a
// register a smaller value is.  Eg. If a value is in a register other than
// its default location (e.g. an SI value in the lower word of an SPU
// register), then this distinction will be via a pgo_mode_e value.
// One could try to keep things more orthogonal, and something like that can
// certainly be built on top of pgo_mode_e, but w.r.t. externalizing GCC
// values, there's just too much randomness so some form of enumeration seems
// to be ultimately necessary.

